1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,165
When a patient is admitted for ward care, they may

2
00:00:03,165 --> 00:00:05,320
still remain in the Emergency Department —

3
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,928
for example, while waiting for a bed.

4
00:00:09,228 --> 00:00:11,399
Inpatient Pharmacy needs to know where

5
00:00:11,399 --> 00:00:12,828
that patient actually is.

6
00:00:13,228 --> 00:00:15,612
Today, the way to find out is to call ED.

7
00:00:16,012 --> 00:00:18,748
Is the patient still here, or already in the ward?

8
00:00:20,048 --> 00:00:23,110
The patient's location affects Pharmacy's workflow:

9
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:25,872
order processing, verification and dispensing.

10
00:00:26,272 --> 00:00:28,843
Checking manually adds delay, workload, and

11
00:00:28,843 --> 00:00:30,816
the risk of outdated information.

12
00:00:32,116 --> 00:00:33,364
The proposed solution.

13
00:00:33,764 --> 00:00:36,340
For patients planned for ward admission who

14
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:39,155
need to stay in ED, register them in PHIS under

15
00:00:39,155 --> 00:00:41,012
Kecemasan & Trauma (Admission).

16
00:00:41,412 --> 00:00:44,244
Visit type: Inpatient. Department: Gen Med.

17
00:00:45,544 --> 00:00:47,899
While the patient is still in ED, the

18
00:00:47,899 --> 00:00:51,144
PHIS location shows Kecemasan & Trauma (Admission).

19
00:00:51,544 --> 00:00:54,159
When the patient enters the receiving ward, the

20
00:00:54,159 --> 00:00:56,328
location is updated to the actual ward.

21
00:00:57,628 --> 00:00:59,711
Under the proposal, the update is made in

22
00:00:59,711 --> 00:01:01,388
Visit Management, in eight steps.

23
00:01:01,788 --> 00:01:04,798
Find the patient, edit the visit, select the new ward

24
00:01:04,798 --> 00:01:07,468
location in the Transfer Detail List, and save.

25
00:01:10,628 --> 00:01:14,036
Today, Pharmacy calls ED to ask where the patient is.

26
00:01:14,436 --> 00:01:17,311
Under the proposal, the PHIS location itself shows

27
00:01:17,311 --> 00:01:20,244
whether the patient is still in ED, or in the ward.

28
00:01:21,544 --> 00:01:24,740
The objective: give Inpatient Pharmacy a reliable way to

29
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:27,480
tell whether an admitted patient is still in ED,

30
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:29,884
or has moved to the receiving ward — with

31
00:01:29,884 --> 00:01:31,448
the minimum additional workload.
